# Performance

Prioritize perceived responsiveness.

Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

Do not recreate expensive objects on every render.

Use memoization only when it provides measurable or meaningful value.

Do not optimize prematurely.

Drawing interactions are performance-sensitive.

Do not update unrelated components during pointer movement.

Avoid storing rapidly changing drawing state in global state.

Large drawings should not cause the entire screen to re-render.

Lists must use appropriate virtualization when necessary.

Images and assets should be handled efficiently.